    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 41 pytest cases covering the spec rules. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (41 passed). The implementation splits each member on `/` and `\\`, drops empty and `.` segments, and resolves `..` against a stack, raising `UnsafePathError` if it would climb above the destination. It also rejects NUL characters, absolute paths, and leading drive prefixes such as `C:` and `c:x`, and it rejects members that normalise to nothing. Directory entries (names ending in a separator) are validated but left out of the result. File members whose normalised paths match case-insensitively raise an error, and the function returns the full plan only after every member has been checked. The destination's trailing slashes are stripped, so `\"/\"` becomes the root. The `UnsafePathError` class and the function signature are unchanged. Two choices the spec left open: a non-string `dest` raises `ValueError` along with an empty one, and a non-string member raises `TypeError`. I did not install anything or create files outside `solution.py` and `tests/`.",
